    seed_window_winit_substring_lane_gate_2026-11-26, fixing, p3sweep2-20261127, 2026-11-27T18:02:40Z, 2026-11-27T18:02:40Z, open, "wave8"

    seed_window_winit_substring_lane_gate_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-61127: reproduced with SIMPLE_ENGINE_RECEIPT=1 - a comment mentioning window_winit and a string literal window_winit were both mis-diverted to the interpreter (engine=interpreter demoted=yes reason=jit-unsafe-graphics), while a real use std.io.window_winit import diverted correctly. Root cause: src/compiler_rust/driver/src/exec_core.rs:2062 source_uses_jit_unsafe_graphics_runtime returned source.contains(window_winit) on the raw entry-file text. Fix: same function parses the entry file with the already-imported simple_parser::Parser and diverts only when a use-family top-level declaration (UseStmt/MultiUse/ExportUseStmt/CommonUseStmt) names window_winit as an exact module path segment or single/aliased/group import target (new helpers item_imports_window_winit, import_names_window_winit, import_target_names_window_winit); a parse failure at gate time falls back to the old substring divert (conservative); the SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter escape hatch untouched. Spec test/01_unit/compiler/seed_window_winit_substring_lane_gate_spec.spl (SIMPLE_BINARY convention): RED 2/4 on the pre-fix seed (comment + string rows), GREEN 4/4 on the fixed scratch; engine-receipt checker pair fixtures updated (the demoting half now uses a REAL import - the old string-literal trigger was exactly the bug; caught my own first rewording self-demoting under the old gate); cargo test -p simple-driver --lib exec_core 42 passed 0 failed; check-engine-receipt-discriminates.shs PASS 10 assertions on both binaries. Residuals: the gate inspects the entry file's own declarations only - transitive winit imports through intermediate modules are not detected (the old substring gate had the same blind spot; the doc's ideal resolved-import-closure remains undone); source_uses_cli_args is still substring-based (out of scope, noted in spec header); the hybrid-interp-splice per-function demotions are a separate mechanism. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/seed_window_winit_substring_lane_gate_spec.spl prevention=test/fixtures/engine_receipt/demote_graphics_text.spl"
